    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed anchor at 82.05. Facing a favorable 5.24 xERA in Quintana, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a solid BvP history, positioning him for a ceiling game in a shallow category like stolen bases. Joining him in the elite tier is **Zach McKinstry** (65.79), whose score is heavily buoyed by a 16% park factor and the premium leadoff spot against Young. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (69.92) remains a high-floor play against P\u00e9rez, leveraging a consistent .379 xwOBA and a prime #1 order placement to drive run production in what should be a productive outing.\n\nStrategic adjustments for today include prioritizing the platoon advantages of **Josh Naylor** (72.02) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (56.94), who both command significant boosts from favorable splits against their respective right-handed matchups. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Jose Caballero** (47.06); while his utility as a stolen base threat is usually vital, the combination of a difficult matchup against Rasmussen and negative environmental factors\u2014specifically wind\u2014pushed him just below the threshold required to crack the starting nine. We continue to monitor the IL status of **Mickey Moniak**, whose absence leaves a void in our outfield depth that keeps players like **Tyler Soderstrom** firmly in the mix.\n\nWhile our lineup is set, we are keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing** (51.29) and **Brice Turang** (49.06), as both face \"Elite Hold\" pitchers today. These catchers and middle infielders will need to navigate the efficiency traps set by Sproat and Yamamoto respectively, as their high pickoff/hold tendencies specifically penalize our pursuit of the stolen base category. Despite the benching of **Carson Williams** and **Kyle Karros** due to lower order positioning and SP skill metrics, we are prepared to rotate in **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Alex Freeland**, or **Henry Bolte** should any mid-game lineup changes or injury notifications emerge from the dugout.",
